    "description": "Horizon New Energy is Copenhagen Infrastructure Partners' Canadian renewable-development platform. CIP launched Horizon in November 2023 with approximately 1.2 GW of Alberta solar, wind and battery-storage projects. Horizon lists the 450 MWac Aira Solar development near Seven Persons, Alberta as one of its projects; Aira is therefore an underlying project and associated SPVs rather than a second manager-level PortCo. Alberta registry records identify CI V Horizon New Energy Devco Ltd and CI V Aira entities, including a March 2025 internal amalgamation into CI V Aira Holdco Ltd. The project has received AESO connection and Alberta Utilities Commission approvals and remained active in AESO's August 2026 project list, but a final investment decision, financing close, construction start, offtaker and commercial-operation date were not publicly disclosed. No third-party platform sale, Aira transfer or signed pending exit was identified through August 19, 2026.",
